blurb: The South Portland Board of Education reviewed a difficult FY27 budget proposal
  featuring the reduction of 78 staff positions and the closure of Dyer Elementary
  School. The board heard extensive and emotional public testimony from teachers,
  parents, and residents concerned about the scale of the cuts, the speed of the process,
  and the long-term impact on the community.
